   "reposts": 28,
   "replies": 26,
   "created_at": "2026-08-02T18:35:50.986Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/carnage4life.bsky.social/post/3ms4msiobbs26",
   "image": "img/2026-08-04/f0f0dadfdc49db8b.webp",
   "external": "",
   "query": "LLM"
  },
  {
   "text": "Has anyone tried using an AI agent to destroy other AI agents and take down data centers yet? 🤔",
   "handle": "dark1x.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "John Linneman",
   "likes": 170,
   "reposts": 8,
   "replies": 21,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T08:01:52.310Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/dark1x.bsky.social/post/3ms5ztrmosc2s",
   "image": "",
   "external": "",
   "query": "AI agent"
  },
  {
   "text": "ChatGPT-maker OpenAI disclosed that one of its cutting-edge artificial intelligence systems had escaped from a controlled testing environment and hacked into another technology company.\n\nHere’s how that attack happened:",
   "handle": "washingtonpost.com",
   "display_name": "The Washington Post",
   "likes": 115,
   "reposts": 34,
   "replies": 14,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T02:00:13.925130202Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/washingtonpost.com/post/3ms5fn4h5li2u",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/interactive/2026/07/30/timeline-cyberattack-by-openais-ai-agent-shows-its-sophistication/?utm_campaign=wp_main&utm_source=bluesky&utm_medium=social",
   "query": "OpenAI"
  },
  {
   "text": "🧵 Snopes pored over hundreds of pages of documents to confirm that Anthropic bought millions of books in bulk and destructively scanned them to train its AI model.",
   "handle": "snopes.com",
   "display_name": "Snopes",
   "likes": 74,
   "reposts": 46,
   "replies": 4,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T21:59:01.846Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/snopes.com/post/3ms7imqgfvm22",
   "image": "img/2026-08-04/064ef2ee9825ef88.webp",
   "external": "",
   "query": "Anthropic"
  },
  {
   "text": "Oracle has become the poster child for the AI bubble.\n\nIt has $130B in debt and is taking on hundreds of billions more in data-center obligations based on a $300B contract with OpenAI over 5 years.\n\nThe problem is many doubt OpenAI will make anywhere close to enough money to pay up.",
   "handle": "carnage4life.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "Dare Obasanjo",
   "likes": 103,
   "reposts": 13,
   "replies": 7,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T05:38:50.645Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/carnage4life.bsky.social/post/3ms5rtzj3kc2j",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/31/magazine/larry-ellison-ai-oracle.html?smid=nytcore-android-share",
   "query": "OpenAI"
  },
  {
   "text": "Lawfare's reporters, like @rparloff.bsky.social, @annabower.bsky.social, and @mollyroberts.bsky.social, show up to the hearings, from Anthropic v. DOD to NPR v. Trump, to bring you minute-by-minute detail of what happened. \n\nThat work isn't free. Help fund it: www.lawfaremedia.org/about/support",
   "handle": "lawfaremedia.org",
   "display_name": "Lawfare",
   "likes": 75,
   "reposts": 23,
   "replies": 0,
   "created_at": "2026-08-02T21:00:41.304Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lawfaremedia.org/post/3ms4uvig2h42f",
   "image": "img/2026-08-04/1e0198c462d386a0.webp",
   "external": "",
   "query": "Anthropic"
  },
  {
   "text": "4/ It doesn’t stop there. Oracle borrows to build data centers for OpenAI. OpenAI promises to pay Oracle later with money it does not have yet. Microsoft owns a slice of OpenAI while also selling it computing power. Everyone is on every side of the table.",
   "handle": "digitalwarrior.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "Digital Warrior - Combat Disinfo",
   "likes": 50,
   "reposts": 21,
   "replies": 2,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T00:39:53.730Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/digitalwarrior.bsky.social/post/3ms5b5hkbos2z",
   "image": "",
   "external": "",
   "query": "OpenAI"
  },
  {
   "text": "Captain Калугин Евгений Сергеевич (Kalugin Evgeny Sergeevich), commander of a company of the 1198th Motor Rifle Regiment, was eliminated in Ukraine.\nThe photo in the obituary bears the Gemini AI watermark.",
   "handle": "killedinukraine.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "KIU • Russian Officers killed in Ukraine",
   "likes": 84,
   "reposts": 4,
   "replies": 1,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T11:00:21.456Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/killedinukraine.bsky.social/post/3ms6dswo32c2u",
   "image": "img/2026-08-04/80450ba525687e98.webp",
   "external": "",
   "query": "Gemini"
  },
  {
   "text": "3/ Now make the shops enormous. Nvidia invests billions in OpenAI. OpenAI turns around and spends that money renting Nvidia’s chips. Nvidia records it as a giant sale. The cash left one pocket and landed back in the other, relabeled as growth.",
   "handle": "digitalwarrior.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "Digital Warrior - Combat Disinfo",
   "likes": 51,
   "reposts": 20,
   "replies": 2,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T00:39:53.729Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/digitalwarrior.bsky.social/post/3ms5b5hkapk2z",
   "image": "",
   "external": "",
   "query": "OpenAI"
  },
  {
   "text": "today I took a photo of the broken part on my phone and Google Gemini instantly gave me instructions on replacing it and an eBay link to buy the replacement part for like $7.",
   "handle": "mtsw.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "mtsw",
   "likes": 88,
   "reposts": 1,
   "replies": 6,
   "created_at": "2026-08-02T22:37:57.890Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mtsw.bsky.social/post/3ms52dgm5yk2x",
   "image": "",
   "external": "",
   "query": "Gemini"
  },
  {
   "text": "Many don't see how much AI has changed recently. Coding agents aren't just chatbots.\n\nWe can’t deal with the challenges of AI if we don’t understand it.\n\nHere's a post to provide some evidence (Claude doing small ML experiments) and form intuitions. \n\ndavidpreichert.substack.com/p/if-you-hav...\n\n🧵..",
   "handle": "david-p-reichert.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "David P. Reichert",
   "likes": 72,
   "reposts": 7,
   "replies": 6,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T08:55:18.516Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/david-p-reichert.bsky.social/post/3ms64tdcdds2s",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://davidpreichert.substack.com/p/if-you-havent-recently-used-claude",
   "query": "Claude AI"
  },
  {
   "text": "@duckduckgo.com is having user survey of why people are going to Duck.ai.\n\nSample page below, I also pay for/rely on Gemini, but these are some ways DDG stands out\n\n(Yes, I know, in some circs it's useful for Gemini/etc know context of your past queries. But nice to escape panopticon.)",
   "handle": "jfallows.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "James Fallows",
   "likes": 66,
   "reposts": 8,
   "replies": 6,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T15:55:02.458Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/jfallows.bsky.social/post/3ms6ubulcns2w",
   "image": "img/2026-08-04/e9960b6bf14f40db.webp",
   "external": "",
   "query": "Gemini"
  },
  {
   "text": "contrast that with this lecture by Terence Tao on how to address LLM-driven changes in your field but hold onto disciplinary values teorth.github.io/tao-web/slid...",
   "handle": "ftrain.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "Paul Ford",
   "likes": 60,
   "reposts": 5,
   "replies": 2,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T18:03:38.400Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/ftrain.bsky.social/post/3ms73ht35c22u",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://teorth.github.io/tao-web/slides/age-of-ai-icm-2026.pdf",
   "query": "LLM"
  },
  {
   "text": "People complain about employers wanting to replace them with AI then fall into the bad habit of responding to questions with “Claude said…” or sharing AI slop documents. \n\nThey fail to realize that they’re making the case that they should be replaced with AI. Your coworkers can prompt Claude too.",
   "handle": "carnage4life.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "Dare Obasanjo",
   "likes": 53,
   "reposts": 6,
   "replies": 3,
   "created_at": "2026-08-03T13:20:09.336Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/carnage4life.bsky.social/post/3ms6lmvxpa225",
   "image": "",
